/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Procedure: Step 1 : Start the program. Step 2 : Declare the required varibles like n, marks[n][3], i, j, avg, tot=0. Step 3 : Read the no. of students. Step 4 : Use nested loop to get input marks and store them in 2D array. Step 5 : Use a loop to calculate total marks. Step 6 : Print the total marks for each student. Step 7 : For each subject initialize sum=0. Step 8 : Use a loop to calculate the sum of marks of all students for that subject. Step 9 : Compute average using avg=\(float\)sum/n and display the average marks of each subject . Step 10: Stop the program.)
/E (Procedure: Step 1 : Start the program. Step 2 : Declare the required varibles like n, marks[n][3], i, j, avg, tot=0. Step 3 : Read the no. of students. Step 4 : Use nested loop to get input marks and store them in 2D array. Step 5 : Use a loop to calculate total marks. Step 6 : Print the total marks for each student. Step 7 : For each subject initialize sum=0. Step 8 : Use a loop to calculate the sum of marks of all students for that subject. Step 9 : Compute average using avg=\(float\)sum/n and display the average marks of each subject . Step 10: Stop the program.)
