<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Procedure: step 1: start the program  step 2: Declare two character arrays first and last to store the names. step 3: Use scanf\(\) to read the first name and last name from the user. step 4: Use strlen\(\) to calculate the length the length of both strings.  step 5: Display the length using printf\(\)  step 6: Use strcmp\(\) to compare the two strings\(\).  step 7: If both are equal, print "Names are equal".  step 8: Use strcat\(\) to concatenate the first name and last name.  step 9: display the concatenated strings as the username.  step 10: end the program)
/E (Procedure: step 1: start the program  step 2: Declare two character arrays first and last to store the names. step 3: Use scanf\(\) to read the first name and last name from the user. step 4: Use strlen\(\) to calculate the length the length of both strings.  step 5: Display the length using printf\(\)  step 6: Use strcmp\(\) to compare the two strings\(\).  step 7: If both are equal, print "Names are equal".  step 8: Use strcat\(\) to concatenate the first name and last name.  step 9: display the concatenated strings as the username.  step 10: end the program)
